          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Visit: belly getting bigger",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-01-17T14:20",
              "body": "He messaged that his pants don't close anymore. About 2 months of the belly slowly growing and feeling tight, uncomfortable after meals. Appetite off. No nausea or vomiting, bowels unchanged, no fever, no belly pain to speak of. Taking both diuretics daily. Hasn't been anywhere, no one sick at home or work. Drinking the same.\n\nBP 98/60 HR 66 afebrile. Weight up from fall. Abdomen tense-ish, distended, fluid wave and shifting dullness, mildly uncomfortable to deep palpation, no rebound. No asterixis. Mild ankle edema.\n\nA/P: More ascites. Ultrasound this week (also covers his 6-month surveillance) plus AFP, and labs today. Spoke with his GI office — they can see him in 3 weeks with a tap in clinic; sooner through the ED if fever, pain, confusion or bleeding. Not changing diuretics before GI weighs in since BP runs low."
            }
