            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Annual Physical",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2023-07-25T08:55",
              "body": "Yearly exam.\n\nSince last year: GI paracentesis in February, ascites portal-hypertensive, no infection. Belly stable since. No bleeding episodes since the 2021 admission. Hep C cured 2022. Testosterone shots every other Friday, no problems. Libido still low; he's made his peace with it. Drinking is back up to about 6 a night after a stressful spring at work. AUDIT-C 10. Mood okay; PHQ-2 0.\n\nExam: BP 102/64, HR 61, afebrile. Thin, temporal wasting. Anicteric today. Spider angiomata, palmar erythema. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear bilaterally. Abdomen distended with fluid wave, nontender. No asterixis. Trace edema.\n\nPrevention: colonoscopy 2022 (next 2032). Shingrix done. Flu yearly. Tdap 2016. Still no hep A/B or pneumococcal vaccine.\n\nPlan:\n- Cirrhosis/portal HTN/ascites — continue meds; labs; surveillance US + AFP ordered.\n- Testosterone: level, Hct, PSA today.\n- AUD — offered referral again; declined. Asked him to at least keep it under where it was last fall.\n- RTC 3 months."
            }
