              "body": "Annual visit.\n\nInterval: ID in January — hep C still cured, flagged his vaccine gaps; PCV20 and hep A/B series started here in Feb/March. No bleeding. Belly up and down with salt. Fatigue in the afternoons. Still 6 beers a night, AUDIT-C 10. Not interested in treatment; \"I know, I know.\" PHQ-2 1.\n\nExam: BP 98/62, HR 64, afebrile, weight about the same. Chronically ill-looking, thin arms. Faint scleral yellowing in daylight. Spider angiomata chest, palmar erythema. Heart regular. Lungs clear. Abdomen distended, fluid wave, nontender. 1+ ankle edema. No asterixis, alert and oriented.\n\nVaccines: hep A #2 and hep B #3 today — both series complete.\n\nPlan:\n- Cirrhosis/portal HTN/ascites: continue regimen. Labs and AFP drawn today; US ordered for this week.\n- Kallmann syndrome: testosterone level, Hct, PSA.\n- AUD: remains the main driver. Discussed again what continued drinking means for bleeding and liver failure, and that I'm here when he is ready.\n- RTC November."
